        "advisory_url": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-25681",
        "description": "A flaw in dnsmasq forward query logic allows remote attackers to spoof DNS replies and execute cache poisoning attacks due to insufficient entropy in query transaction IDs.",
        "workaround": "Enable DNSSEC verification or redirect local DNS queries through encrypted DNS-over-HTTPS (DoH) upstream proxies.",
        "applicable_architectures": [],
        "last_audit_date": "2026-11-15"
      },
      {
        "cve_id": "CVE-2020-25682",
